WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.492
In 24 hours, I built
an artificial intelligence agent.

2
00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:11.654
The first Philips AI Hackathon LATAM:
91 teams from all over Latin America.

3
00:00:12.016 --> 00:00:14.195
My team won.
Six months earlier,

4
00:00:14.235 --> 00:00:16.048
I joined as an intern.

5
00:00:16.088 --> 00:00:17.488
I'm Martín Bundy.

6
00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.388
I study Industrial Engineering and AI.

7
00:00:24.788 --> 00:00:27.688
And I use AI to solve real problems.

8
00:00:27.988 --> 00:00:30.714
I'm from Panama.
As a kid, whenever I got stuck,

9
00:00:30.754 --> 00:00:33.054
I found my own way forward.

10
00:00:33.138 --> 00:00:36.638
Today I do the same,
with processes, data and agents.

11
00:00:36.988 --> 00:00:39.588
At Philips, I work in
operational procurement,

12
00:00:39.938 --> 00:00:43.438
the team that moves every purchase
from start to finish.

13
00:00:43.588 --> 00:00:45.148
That's when it clicked.

14
00:00:45.188 --> 00:00:48.166
Industrial Engineering taught me to work
with very different processes,

15
00:00:48.206 --> 00:00:50.826
and to understand
everything that can happen

16
00:00:50.866 --> 00:00:52.508
in a large operation.

17
00:00:52.548 --> 00:00:57.058
My question is always how to optimize it:
reduce lead times, improve KPIs.

18
00:00:57.388 --> 00:01:01.798
At Philips, I tracked every purchase
with 4 KPIs and built a no-code dashboard.

19
00:01:01.838 --> 00:01:03.538
No more manual reports.

20
00:01:03.788 --> 00:01:06.688
With AI, I automate:
agents and custom-built software.

21
00:01:07.338 --> 00:01:08.976
AI helps me with everything:

22
00:01:09.016 --> 00:01:11.808
from my daily life to the
processes at Philips.

23
00:01:11.848 --> 00:01:15.465
In 2025, I led the AI integration
for Conecta Panamá:

24
00:01:15.505 --> 00:01:18.115
a citizen super app, in two weeks.

25
00:01:18.704 --> 00:01:23.104
I did the AI, the design, the interface,
the backend and the debugging.

26
00:01:23.535 --> 00:01:24.635
First place.

27
00:01:24.905 --> 00:01:27.119
The Municipality's digital innovation team

28
00:01:27.159 --> 00:01:28.319
wanted to apply it,

29
00:01:28.359 --> 00:01:31.559
and we sat down to plan
taking it nationwide.

30
00:01:31.871 --> 00:01:33.890
I trained a university
assistant with BERT:

31
00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:37.161
it answers the questions
that used to come in by email.

32
00:01:37.201 --> 00:01:40.061
I presented a logistics copilot live
at Expo Logística,

33
00:01:40.101 --> 00:01:43.011
in front of transport,
cargo and 3PL companies.

34
00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:46.803
At Philips, I built an agent
that answers in seconds

35
00:01:46.843 --> 00:01:48.843
and cites the exact source.

36
00:01:50.103 --> 00:01:54.005
Last year, only Panama competed.
This year, all of Latin America.

37
00:01:54.693 --> 00:01:57.391
I led the team and built
all of PO Guru's AI

38
00:01:57.431 --> 00:01:58.831
in 24 hours.

39
00:01:59.593 --> 00:02:00.993
A 4-minute pitch.

40
00:02:01.093 --> 00:02:04.293
First place in Panama,
out of about 30 teams.

41
00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:07.010
In the final, against the region's best,

42
00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:08.150
first place.

43
00:02:08.404 --> 00:02:10.564
I learned to work under pressure.

44
00:02:10.604 --> 00:02:15.004
I like to understand what people need,
connect the pieces, test, and improve.

45
00:02:18.254 --> 00:02:19.166
What I learn, I teach:

46
00:02:19.206 --> 00:02:22.476
on tincho.ia, I explain AI
and agents from scratch.

47
00:02:23.104 --> 00:02:26.904
My CV is a website I
designed and built with AI.

48
00:02:27.804 --> 00:02:30.704
And I directed this film with agents, too.

49
00:02:35.204 --> 00:02:37.764
To me, AI is already the present.

50
00:02:37.804 --> 00:02:39.804
Everything is changing really fast,

51
00:02:40.804 --> 00:02:44.004
and learning to build
with agents is a wave.

52
00:02:45.054 --> 00:02:48.254
You either catch it, or
you get left behind.

53
00:02:54.054 --> 00:02:56.826
I like to dream big.
I don't box myself into one thing.

54
00:02:56.866 --> 00:02:59.166
I'm always open to new challenges.

55
00:03:02.054 --> 00:03:03.154
What's next...

56
00:03:04.854 --> 00:03:06.854
...I'll tell you in person.
